## 3. Per-stage subagent configuration (non-negotiable)

```
discrepancy_subagent: per-iteration
discrepancy_score_access: forbidden
discrepancy_prior_iteration_access: forbidden
rule_edit_subagent: per-iteration
rule_edit_baseline_access: forbidden
rule_edit_score_access: forbidden
auditor: per-iteration
auditor_score_access: forbidden
auditor_frequency_reduction: forbidden
```

<!-- These nine lines are non-negotiable. They encode the per-stage
     information-isolation design lock at DESIGN.md §4.2. Each cognitive
     stage in /spp-loop's iteration runs in an isolated subagent with an
     explicit allow-list of inputs; the orchestrator coordinates, it does
     not do cognitive work. Breaking any of these silently weakens the
     methodology.

     Discrepancy subagent (commands/spp-loop.md §4 step 8): produces
     `discrepancy_analysis.md` referencing rows by ID only. Sees the
     current iteration's eval.json, results.json, baseline.csv filtered
     to disagreed dev rows, current prompt, plan.md §2. Does not see
     prior iterations' artifacts.

     Rule-edit subagent (commands/spp-loop.md §4 step 10): produces
     `prompt_v(N+1).md`. Sees current prompt, current discrepancy_analysis.md
     (row IDs only, no row content), plan.md §2, prompt-architect sub-skill.
     Does NOT see baseline.csv, eval.json, or results.json. No row content
     reaches this subagent under any path.

     Auditor (commands/spp-loop.md §4 step 11): the most stringent
     instance. Sees prompt diff, prior discrepancy, plan.md §2, prior
     auditor reviews. Does not see the new iteration's scores. This is
     the design lock that distinguishes spp from automated optimizers;
     breaking it breaks the methodology silently (DESIGN.md §4.2 +
     CLAUDE.md §8).

     Frequency reduction is forbidden as an "improvement" for the
     auditor. If per-iteration cost becomes an adoption barrier
     post-v1, the correct escape valve is BATCH AUDITING (auditor
     reviews the last N iterations as a group, still without score
     access), not "audit every N iterations." See DESIGN.md §7.1
     non-goals.

     The Phase 4 template linter verifies these nine lines are
     literally present and unmodified before a loop_spec.md is
     accepted. Do not parameterize them. -->

